{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145790",
      "title": "Module Summary",
      "lectureOrder": 291,
      "videoOrder": 271,
      "sourceHash": "e362b5bb72bf87e3a69aabb1c7ccdbcc5cf52a7b42f7e3be7742b503f7cef09d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.299,
          "end": 4.43,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] Now this was a long module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.43,
          "end": 7.06,
          "en": "with a lot of key concepts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.06,
          "end": 9.3,
          "en": "In general, this module was about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.3,
          "end": 13.14,
          "en": "how Next.js pre-renders pages for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.14,
          "end": 15.42,
          "en": "so that if we view at a page source",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.42,
          "end": 18.64,
          "en": "we have some data in that page source,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.64,
          "end": 21.17,
          "en": "some data which is there right from the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.17,
          "end": 23.07,
          "en": "and which is there for all the visible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.07,
          "end": 25.27,
          "en": "to search engine crawlers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.27,
          "end": 26.58,
          "en": "which is a key difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.58,
          "end": 30.42,
          "en": "to standard React apps without service side rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.42,
          "end": 31.83,
          "en": "Now you did learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.83,
          "end": 36.62,
          "en": "that out of the box Next.js pre-renders your pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.62,
          "end": 39.03,
          "en": "It does that automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.03,
          "end": 43.26,
          "en": "but you can also force it to do so by adding getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 45.12,
          "en": "because you add this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.12,
          "end": 49.83,
          "en": "whenever you also wanna pre-fetch data for your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.83,
          "end": 53.1,
          "en": "So if your page component doesn't need any data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.1,
          "end": 56.63,
          "en": "of course you never add getStaticProps typically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.63,
          "end": 60.25,
          "en": "because it doesn't add anything to the page then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.25,
          "end": 62.8,
          "en": "but if your page does needs data like the list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.8,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "of products here, then you add getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 70.74,
          "en": "So that during the build process, this data is pre-fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.74,
          "end": 74.13,
          "en": "and available for the page when it's pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.13,
          "end": 78.143,
          "en": "so that the pre-rendered page contains pre-fetched data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.37,
          "end": 81.65,
          "en": "Since geStaticProps executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.65,
          "end": 83.47,
          "en": "during the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.47,
          "end": 86.53999999999999,
          "en": "you can execute node js code in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.53999999999999,
          "end": 88.87,
          "en": "which wouldn't run in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.87,
          "end": 90.39,
          "en": "For example you can get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.39,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "to the file system and read data from files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 97.66,
          "en": "Since data can get outdated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.66,
          "end": 100.09,
          "en": "after the pages were pre-generated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.09,
          "end": 103.22,
          "en": "you can also add the revalidate key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.22,
          "end": 107.14,
          "en": "in the object you return from inside getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.14,
          "end": 108.58,
          "en": "to tell Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.58,
          "end": 112.44,
          "en": "that this page should be regenerated again and again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.44,
          "end": 116.25999999999999,
          "en": "even after the page was built and deployed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.25999999999999,
          "end": 121.26,
          "en": "at most every x seconds here at most once every 10 seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.46,
          "end": 124.42,
          "en": "Therefore getStaticProps is great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.42,
          "end": 128.563,
          "en": "for ensuring that you are pre-rendering pages with data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.42,
          "end": 133.63,
          "en": "If you have dynamic pages with a dynamic parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.63,
          "end": 138.63,
          "en": "then you also need to let Next.js know how many instances",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.06,
          "end": 141.42000000000002,
          "en": "of that page should be pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.42000000000002,
          "end": 144.54,
          "en": "because it could be an infinite amount in theory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.54,
          "end": 147.05,
          "en": "You do that with getStaticPaths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.05,
          "end": 149.47,
          "en": "and you need to add this when using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.47,
          "end": 152.78,
          "en": "getStaticProps on such a dynamic page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.78,
          "end": 154.44,
          "en": "Otherwise we'll get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.44,
          "end": 158.86,
          "en": "because Next.js doesn't know how many pages to prepare.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.86,
          "end": 162.6,
          "en": "GetStaticPaths returns an object with a paths' key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 162.6,
          "end": 166.7,
          "en": "which holds an array of param objects in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.7,
          "end": 169.99,
          "en": "where you basically just make Next.js aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.99,
          "end": 172.37,
          "en": "of all the parameter values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.37,
          "end": 175.82,
          "en": "for this dynamic page that should be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.82,
          "end": 178.45,
          "en": "for pre-rendering a page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.45,
          "end": 181.1,
          "en": "And you can also reach out to a file system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.1,
          "end": 184.43,
          "en": "or database or whatever you need to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.43,
          "end": 187.43,
          "en": "and when you do that Next.js will pre-generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.43,
          "end": 191.27,
          "en": "all the paths so all the instances of that page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 191.27,
          "end": 195.32,
          "en": "for the paths you tell it to pre-render.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.32,
          "end": 197.46,
          "en": "It will then call getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.46,
          "end": 200.24,
          "en": "for every page instance that it creates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.24,
          "end": 202.85,
          "en": "you can access the params there as you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.85,
          "end": 206.24,
          "en": "and then you can fetch and prepare the data there just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.24,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "as it's needed, return that to the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 213.47,
          "en": "and then last but not least Next.js will execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.47,
          "end": 216.5,
          "en": "this component function in the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.5,
          "end": 220.64,
          "en": "or on the server to pre-render this page as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 220.64,
          "end": 222.663,
          "en": "with the appropriate data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.09,
          "end": 228.18,
          "en": "Sometimes you don't wanna pre-build during the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.18,
          "end": 230.71,
          "en": "and even when using revalidate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.71,
          "end": 233.92000000000002,
          "en": "the data might not be updated enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.92000000000002,
          "end": 236.48,
          "en": "Instead you really might want to run logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.48,
          "end": 240.13,
          "en": "for every incoming request either because you need access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.13,
          "end": 244.14,
          "en": "to the request or because the data changes all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.14,
          "end": 247.7,
          "en": "In such cases, you can use getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.7,
          "end": 251.07,
          "en": "It's an alternative and unlike getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.07,
          "end": 254.89,
          "en": "this really runs on the server and only on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.89,
          "end": 257.53,
          "en": "not during the build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.53,
          "end": 261.62,
          "en": "Here you can get access to the request and response objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 261.62,
          "end": 264.99,
          "en": "to the real node request and response objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.99,
          "end": 267.77,
          "en": "and you still return props to component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 267.77,
          "end": 269.58,
          "en": "which is then pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.58,
          "end": 272.92,
          "en": "but pre-rendered on the fly on the Server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.73,
          "end": 277.28,
          "en": "You can also do that for dynamic pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.28,
          "end": 279.89,
          "en": "and here you don't need getStaticPaths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.89,
          "end": 282.6,
          "en": "because this now really does only execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.6,
          "end": 285.87,
          "en": "when it's needed not in advance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.87,
          "end": 289.22,
          "en": "However sometimes that's all not what you are looking for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 289.22,
          "end": 291.40999999999997,
          "en": "Sometimes you really need to fetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.40999999999997,
          "end": 295.11,
          "en": "from inside the client or you wanna to combine pre-rendering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 295.11,
          "end": 297.32,
          "en": "with client site data fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.32,
          "end": 299.94,
          "en": "And that's what we saw in the last lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.94,
          "end": 303.78,
          "en": "You can also still write regular React code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 303.78,
          "end": 307.34,
          "en": "regular React JavaScript code for fetching data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.34,
          "end": 309.46,
          "en": "in your component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.46,
          "end": 312.66,
          "en": "and this code will then not be executed on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 312.66,
          "end": 315.32,
          "en": "even though the page will still be pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.32,
          "end": 317.21,
          "en": "but this code will be skipped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.21,
          "end": 319.59,
          "en": "since its inside of useEffect typically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.59,
          "end": 322.56,
          "en": "instead you'll just get some Snapshot of your page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 322.56,
          "end": 323.86,
          "en": "which is then returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 323.86,
          "end": 327.25,
          "en": "and that code really only runs in the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 327.25,
          "end": 329.79,
          "en": "So when a visitor visits the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 329.79,
          "end": 333.57,
          "en": "here you can also consider using the useSWR hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 333.57,
          "end": 336.57,
          "en": "since that can make writing that code a bit easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 336.57,
          "end": 340.18,
          "en": "and since that is a feature rich custom hook built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.18,
          "end": 342.99,
          "en": "by the Next.js team which for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 342.99,
          "end": 346.48,
          "en": "also automatically re-fetches data if you will lose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 346.48,
          "end": 349.97,
          "en": "and regain focus in your browser tab.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 349.97,
          "end": 351.90999999999997,
          "en": "So that can also be nice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 351.90999999999997,
          "end": 354.54,
          "en": "And as you saw you can even still combine that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 354.54,
          "end": 357.54,
          "en": "with preparing and pre-fetching data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 357.54,
          "end": 359.86,
          "en": "And therefore this was a long module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 359.86,
          "end": 363.24,
          "en": "but data fetching and pre-rendering of pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 363.24,
          "end": 368.24,
          "en": "with pre-fetched data is another key aspect off Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 369.39,
          "end": 374,
          "en": "The file-based routing was nice and already a great feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 374,
          "end": 377.31,
          "en": "but this here pre-fetching and pre-rendering,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 377.31,
          "end": 378.37,
          "en": "that's the feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 378.37,
          "end": 381.86,
          "en": "which really makes Next.js super powerful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 381.86,
          "end": 385.87,
          "en": "because now it's easy to optimize pages for search engines,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 385.87,
          "end": 389.75,
          "en": "it's easy to show users some data right from the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 389.75,
          "end": 394.05,
          "en": "and you can still apply everything you know about React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 394.05,
          "end": 397.05,
          "en": "And therefore let's now apply what we learned here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 397.05,
          "end": 400.52,
          "en": "to our demo project in the next section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 400.52,
          "end": 403.35,
          "en": "before we then dig deeper into Next again",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
